	(text_box "1. Function: J5 and J6 are the carrier's two DF40C-80DP plugs (bottom side since layout V5, 25 Nov 2026, at the Carrier V6 LDO plug site on the west edge; top side at the MC1 edge in layouts V1-V4). Layout V7 (routed): each plug row leaves on its own layer (J5 even pins L8, J5 odd pins L7, J6 even pins L2, J6 odd pins L1 through a via in the pad), and each rail reaches its J5 pin on L8 and its J6 pin on L1 from one through via at the rail entry, where its two 1 uF capacitors sit (one on each side of the board). They mate the Option B router V3 receptacles J5/J6 (DF40C-80DS, router B.Cu) pin n to pin n, 1.5 mm stack, and carry 128 signal contacts (121 nets; each *_SHARED line reaches both plugs from one FPGA pin), the nine ASIC rails, AGND, GND and ASIC_AC_IN. Each of the eight split rails is tied J5 even pin to J6 odd pin on one regulator net (J5.34/36/38/40/50/52/54/56 to J6.33/35/37/39/49/51/53/55); VDD_CGEN is J5.1 + J6.2 (drawn over the top); AGND J5.42/44 = J6.41/43; GND J5.3/5/46/48 = J6.4/6/45/47. NT1 (between the AGND and GND ties) is the only AGND-GND bond of the whole head; layout rule: place NT1 between the AGND returns of the regulator input capacitors (sheet ASIC_Rails) and the plug AGND pins, as on the V24 PCB (NT1 at 100.58, 121.0 on L6, between the plug fan and the regulators), not at the plug edge, and keep those AGND input-capacitor returns next to NT1. TP20 provides a local AGND probe pad beside the plug-side rail test pads (schematic V4). ASIC_AC_IN (J5.69, J6.70) is tied by a label only: no FPGA pin and no load on the carrier.\n\n2. Source / changes: Pin contract PIN_MAP_B_V2.csv (router J5 pin n = ASIC port J3 pin n; router J6 pin 2k+1 = ASIC port J4 pin 2k+2) and SYNTHESIS.md sections 3 and 6 (24 Nov 2026), cross-checked with pin table V3 (XEM8305_PIN_TABLE_V3, the V3 XDC; schematic V3 changed only the XEM-side pins, not these plug pins) and the V24 J3/J4 nets: 0 differences (inventory/I3_interface_spec_V3.csv). Hirose DF40 series data sheet as filed by LCSC for C294544 DF40C-80DP-0.4V(51), https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C294544.pdf (revision, page and land-pattern figure not read here: confirm the 80-pin plug drawing, land pattern and the 0.3 A contact rating used below before layout). Symbol, footprint and fields copied from FPGA-LDO A V24 J3 (DF40C-80DP-0.4V(51), JLC C294544, 5759 orderable, read 25 Nov 2026, 07:22 CST; 10 needed for 5 carriers). Designed by Claude from the contract: V24 J4 was a DS receptacle, carrier J6 is a DP plug; rail, AGND and GND ties and the GND/AGND symbols drawn here; NT1 moved from the V24 VIN entry block (same part and footprint). V24 R6/TP7 (AC_IN default) stay on the router. The DF40C-80DP metal (MP) pads have no net, as on V24 (symbol pins 1-80 only); tying them to GND is open for Howard. Unverified: rail current per contact (one 0.3 A contact per rail per plug), mated contact resistance, and the mechanical holder."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 337.82 97.4 0)
		(size 149.86 51)
