				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "47d0c76c-73e1-560b-9df0-9fc9d8d0a135")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: Seventeen 1 uF 0402 capacitors decouple the ASIC rails at the plug contacts: on each split-rail line one at the J5 end (left: C51-C55, C57-C59) and one at the J6 end (right: C60-C67), plus C56 on the VDD_CGEN bridge (J5.1/J6.2). Fifteen return to AGND; the two DVDD capacitors C54 and C60 return to GND, the ground the ASIC boards decouple DVDD to.\n\n2. Source / changes: Designed by Claude, no manufacturer reference circuit; required by SYNTHESIS.md section 3 (drive-board parts: 17 x 1 uF 0402 C52923, each within about 3 mm of its pin). Part Samsung CL05A105KA5NQNC 1 uF 25 V X5R 0402 (Samsung reference sheet p.1, https://product.samsungsem.com/part/download.do?masterKey=CL05A105KA5NQN&type=specsheet ), JLC Basic C52923 (10063170 orderable, read 25 Nov 2026, 07:22 CST; 85 needed), https://jlcpcb.com/partdetail/C52923 . Changed from V24 block RAIL CAPACITORS AT THE ASIC PORTS: C51 and C53-C57 keep their refs but change from C14445 (10 V) to C52923 (25 V, needed on +/-8.06 V); C52, C58-C67 are new; the VDD_ADC/VDD10/VSS10 port capacitors removed on the LDO board in V28 (Howard, 9 Nov 2026) are back because the contract asks for 17; keeping them is open for Howard (mark DNP if he declines). Deviation from the contract text (rail to AGND): DVDD to GND as V24 V34 (review LDOA-11/-16), because the ASIC DVDD domain returns on digital GND (plug pins 3/5/46/48); open for Howard. Samsung sheet: p.1 ratings, edition as served 24 Nov 2026. Unverified: ASIC-board capacitance and regulator stability with this capacitance at the end of the trace."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 158.75 0)
		(size 134.62 39.6)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c0ae0a4e-9475-5f80-ac9a-001454382352")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: Ten of the seventeen 10k safe-idle resistors sit on J5 lines: R30/R31/R32/R33 (STIM_EN/START/CHB/CLK_SHARED), R16 (FE_RESET_SHARED), R17 (IMP_TST_SHARED), R21 (BOARD3_CLK), R23 (BOARD3_SPI_CLK) and R28 (BOARD3_SPI_LATCH) pull low; R19 pulls CHIP_RESET_SHARED up to ASIC_DVDD so the ASICs stay in reset. They hold the lines while the XEM8305 banks are unpowered (before XEM_PG) or the FPGA is unconfigured; each *_SHARED net is pulled once, here. The other seven: R20, R18, R22 at J6 and R24-R27 between the plugs.\n\n2. Source / changes: Copied from FPGA-LDO A V24 blocks ASIC CONTROL SAFE IDLE (R2-R5, R16-R19) and ASIC CLOCK AND TOP-CHIP SPI SAFE IDLE (R20-R28): Claude design from Gerald's firmware (top_custom.v section 3b holds CHIP_RESET high at boot; spi_programmer.v keeps SCLK idle low and pulses LATCH high) and the ASIC designer's answer C2 (no internal pulls; meeting 12 Nov 2026). Part unchanged: 10k 1 % 0402 Uniroyal 0402WGF1002TCE, JLC Basic C25744 (27090458 orderable, read 25 Nov 2026, 07:22 CST). Changed for Carrier V7 by Claude: V24 R2/R3/R4/R5 renumbered R30/R31/R32/R33 (Carrier V6 uses R2-R5); each resistor drawn on its plug-pin line; the lines are driven by XEM8305 bank 64/84/86 pins (sheet XEM_Power_USB). Unverified: V24 relied on the Frontend tying PUDC_B high; the XEM8305 PUDC_B state is not documented by Opal Kelly and not checked (AMD UG570 UltraScale Configuration, PUDC_B pin description, HTML edition as served 24 Nov 2026, https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug570-ultrascale-configuration ; Opal Kelly https://docs.opalkelly.com/xem8305/ ). If PUDC_B is low, the FPGA pull-ups fight these pull-downs while the FPGA is unconfigured; open for Howard (measure a user pin through 10k to GND on a module with no bitstream). Since the review fix U21 (sheet ASIC_Rails), the ASIC rails stay off until XEM_PG, so R19 no longer feeds an unpowered bank. The 16 FPGA-to-ASIC SPI data lines (ASIC3/4/7/8_SPI_DR/DL, STIM_CHIP1-4_SPI_DR/DL) have no pull, as on V24: with clock and latch held low the ASIC ignores them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 41.91 275.59 0)
		(size 150 43.4)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
