				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "481ee494-fc2c-5301-bb3f-b3425aed3147")
	)
	(text_box "1. Function: R24-R27 hold the top chips' own SPI clocks and latches low while the FPGA is unconfigured or its banks are unpowered: R27 ASIC7_8_TOP_SPI_LATCH (J5.70), R25 ASIC7_8_TOP_SPI_CLK (J5.72), R26 ASIC3_4_TOP_SPI_LATCH (J6.69), R24 ASIC3_4_TOP_SPI_CLK (J6.71).\n\n2. Source / changes: Copied from FPGA-LDO A V24 block ASIC CLOCK AND TOP-CHIP SPI SAFE IDLE (Claude design, review items LDOA-49 and SYS-28; refs and part unchanged: 10k 1 % 0402, JLC C25744, read 25 Nov 2026, 07:22 CST); drawn on their plug-pin lines for Carrier V7. Same basis and the same unverified PUDC_B point as the J5 safe-idle box on the left."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 345.44 406.4 0)
		(size 134.62 22.4)
